  "question": {
    "text": "The frequency distribution of the age of students in a class of 40 students is given below.\n$\\begin{array}{|l|c|c|c|c|l|l|}\n\\hline \\text{Age} & 15 & 16 & 17 & 18 & 19 & 20 \\\\\n\\hline \\text{No of Students} & 5 & 8 & 5 & 12 & x & y \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}$\nIf the mean deviation about the median is 1.25, then $4 x+5 y$ is equal to :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "46",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "43",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "44",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "47",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{x}+\\mathrm{y}=10 \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots .(1) \\\\ & \\text {Median }=18=\\mathrm{M} \\\\ & \\text {M.D. }=\\frac{\\sum \\mathrm{f}_{\\mathrm{i}}\\left|\\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{i}}-\\mathrm{M}\\right|}{\\sum \\mathrm{f}_{\\mathrm{i}}} \\\\ & 1.25=\\frac{36+\\mathrm{x}+2 \\mathrm{y}}{40} \\\\ & \\mathrm{x}+2 \\mathrm{y}=14 \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots .(2) \\\\ & \\text { by (1) & (2) } \\\\ & \\mathrm{x}=6, \\mathrm{y}=4 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow 4 \\mathrm{x}+5 \\mathrm{y}=24+20=44\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{array}{|l|l|l|l|}\n\\hline \\operatorname{Age}\\left(\\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{i}}\\right) & \\mathrm{f} & \\left|\\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{i}}-\\mathrm{M}\\right| & \\mathrm{f}_{\\mathrm{i}}\\left|\\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{i}}-\\mathrm{M}\\right| \\\\\n\\hline 15 & 5 & 3 & 15 \\\\\n\\hline 16 & 8 & 2 & 16 \\\\\n\\hline 17 & 5 & 1 & 5 \\\\\n\\hline 18 & 12 & 0 & 0 \\\\\n\\hline 19 & \\mathrm{x} & 1 & \\mathrm{x} \\\\\n\\hline 20 & \\mathrm{y} & 2 & 2 \\mathrm{y} \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}$"
  }
